= Honors, Awards, and Scholarships

#entry[2026][
#strong[HIDA-Sponsored Participant – The Carpentries Instructor Training], selected for one of 15 annually sponsored training places offered by the Helmholtz Information & Data Science Academy (HIDA) to Helmholtz researchers. The program provides evidence-based training in scientific and data science instruction and leads toward certification as a Carpentries Instructor. Equivalent training value of USD 1.600 (approximately € 1.360; exchange rate 1 USD = 0,85 EUR).
]

#entry[2025][
#strong[Google PhD Fellowship in Health] awarded to support outstanding and innovative research in computer science and related fields, providing total funding of USD 30.000 over two years (approximately € 25.500; exchange rate 1 USD = 0,85 EUR).
]

#entry[2025][
#strong[ISME Scholar Mobility Fund] awarded with funding of € 2.300 for a research period in July 2026 at the Helmholtz Centre for Environmental Research (UFZ) in Leipzig, Germany.
]

#entry[2024][
#strong[J. F. Marar Artificial Intelligence Prize for Undergraduate Research] awarded with a prize of R\$10.500 for the project #emph[BioDeepFuse: Empowering Researchers in Life Sciences with Deep Learning] recognized for academic excellence, social impact, and alignment with the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) (approximately € 1.680; exchange rate 1 R\$ = 0,16 EUR).
]

#entry[2024][
#strong[Prototypes for Humanity Travel Grant] awarded to BioAutoML, selected as a top 100 project among nearly 3.000 global submissions, with funding of USD 760 to support presentation at the international festival in Dubai (approximately € 646; exchange rate 1 USD = 0,85 EUR).
]

